  4. accepted translations -> SFTSample (user=CUDA+porting requirements,
     assistant=reasoning+SYCL); every record also yields an RLPrompt with
     reward.type="code_exec" (the L0/L1 checks are the executable reward)

--dry-run replaces the teacher with 2 hand-written (cuda, sycl) pairs
(vector_add, sgemv from corpus.load_builtin()); L0 runs for real.
--no-teacher emits only RL prompts.

